    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d379-a7">

                <pb facs="0407" n="1085" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg1085"/>

                <head>[Enclosure No. 7.]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States in
                                Japan</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Yedo</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 23, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of yesterday, covering copy of a general order issued by
                    Rear-Admiral Kuper, with the view of providing for the safety of the foreign
                    community in the event of any attack or disturbances at Yokohama.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient, humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. H. PRUYN, <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Resident of the United
                            States in Japan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
